@startuml Composite-Structure
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
title Composite — pattern structure (Design Patterns, p. 164)

class Client

abstract class Component {
  + operation() : void
  + add(c : Component) : void
  + remove(c : Component) : void
  + getChild(index : int) : Component
}
note right of Component
  Declares the interface for objects
  in the composition and implements
  default behavior. Child operations
  are declared HERE — the choice that
  buys transparency (p. 168).
end note

class Leaf {
  + operation() : void
}
note bottom of Leaf
  Has no children.
  Defines behavior for
  primitive objects.
end note

class Composite {
  - children : List<Component>
  + operation() : void
  + add(c : Component) : void
  + remove(c : Component) : void
  + getChild(index : int) : Component
}
note bottom of Composite
  operation() forwards to
  every child — this loop
  IS the pattern:
    for (c : children)
        c.operation();
end note

Client --> Component
Component <|-- Leaf
Component <|-- Composite
Composite o--> "*" Component : children

@enduml
